<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: France braces for fresh nationwide protests over school conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b2329afc76ccba445800d77ef4922ce410ccdac3645cb39ba23d5362d8b02db</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions" /><summary type="html">France faces fresh nationwide demonstrations on Tuesday as students, unions and opposition groups rally over poor school conditions, including teacher shortages and dilapidated buildings. More than 70,000 people protested last Thursday, with around 500 arrests, as authorities warned that violence was intensifying despite a decline in school closures. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia says Europe bought $320 billion in hydrocarbons since 2022</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:206184a7491df0dee6680db51fab9c1feb2f86c0c6d36979a75791da4f7c9dc9</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T03:10:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022" /><summary type="html">Russia said on Monday that European Union countries had bought $320.7 billion worth of its energy resources since 2022, despite sanctions over the war in Ukraine. The figure fuelled tensions as European officials criticised a US deal to import Russian diesel, while Stockholm called for the bloc to use frozen Russian assets to boost support for Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo to enter hospital on Tuesday for surgery on lung nodule this week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c42e19eb0ef8b76e69724141aab51d459427b0c2804c371ce459b5202e598646</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T22:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is expected to undergo surgery to remove a lung nodule this week at Rome’s Gemelli hospital, with doctors anticipating a recovery of about seven days. The 71-year-old pontiff is due to travel to Uruguay, Argentina and Peru on November 6, though the Vatican has not confirmed the operation date.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington', analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20c9001ae0929e85d58a22e41c36ffee74d80b231a27bdda28530bdfc72442f5</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:02:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington', analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:730b57478246ec36bf78e4a3ddc9cd1f56e618fe20f40a46478cc27366ee0011</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary></entry><entry><title>Tehran denies involvement in UK Fairford air base incident as Britain summons Iranian ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce70e601ddc7662c79149afdde9904b8d9d1168993746293517781eec9f53e45</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambassador" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being responsible for a terror-related incident in September at England's Fairford air base, which is used by the United States military. Following Tehran's denial, the British Foreign Office summoned Iran's Ambassador for talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Increasingly evident' Russia won't accept 'energy ceasefire': Zelensky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f342a113c09d0988136ee6d129806b2dd577fed6f5af006be2c367281ec6c556</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:40:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/increasingly-evident-russia-won-t-accept-energy-ceasefire-zelensky" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday it was clear that Russia would not agree to stop hitting energy targets, after US President Donald Trump unilaterally announced a deal between the warring nations. "It is increasingly evident that Russia is unwilling to accept an energy ceasefire proposed by the United States," Zelensky said on social media. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'A lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed' by Trump's Russian diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:971d3b59c361743064620650f1720531d079b9fbb715ad430564e74718bba331</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-lot-of-ukrainians-are-feeling-extremely-betrayed-by-trump-s-russian-diesel-deal" /><summary type="html">Reporting from central Ukraine, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg says that "a lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed by a country that until recently they saw not only as an ally but as a beacon of freedom and democracy, a country whose values they should aspire to. All of that is falling apart very quickly and Ukrainians' admiration for the United States is disintegrating."</summary></entry><entry><title>How has the European Union’s major recovery plan benefited the 27 member states?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b47314fcf8147aa61b74c335f8185b0d75573b2f53499778a0f85d14186ae417</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-_600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe--6b8c747aa05e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-%E2%82%AC600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe" /><summary type="html">The 27 member states of the European Union agreed in July 2020 on a €750 billion post-Covid recovery plan called NextGenerationEU. Its main instrument is the Recovery and Resilience Facility, through which the European Commission has already disbursed €450 billion. The programme is due to come to an end in a few months, and countries must claim and account for the remaining funds.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU warns online platforms over livestreaming US execution planned by Pentagon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc16ba010812a171d5c6a4bf3fb8ebd79ca2dd3f718136e148f64c3d13c8ce70</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:05:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon--559bc068ffcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The European Union warned digital platforms on Monday against livestreaming the execution of Nidal Hasan, a former US Army psychiatrist who is scheduled to be executed by firing squad on December 3 for killing 13 people at a military base in 2009. Under EU rules, platforms have an obligation to moderate shocking and violent content, including capital punishment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO's top US commander warns Russia that any 'foolish' attack on allies would be 'futile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab71a5f04ce7cfe18654aeaae60d2793b0bacc1a34b93c8bfa5a4673e2fd830a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:41:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile--6a6b5384d4d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile" /><summary type="html">NATO's top US military commander in Europe said Monday that any "foolish" attack on the alliance would be "utterly futile", a warning to Russia as European fears grow over the threat from Moscow that includes "hybrid" warfare and cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: NATO's top military commander warns Russia over alleged sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a14e59d256d79abc5a9dd165e690992638933f2b69b677f565465cfe12936264</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:26:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage--36373f6834b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage" /><summary type="html">And as the war in Ukraine continues, Western concerns are growing over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Kiev's wartime backers. NATO's top military commander gave a press conference this Monday from Warsaw. US General Alexus Grynkewich looks set to warn Russia over the alliance’s ability to counter-attack. Analysis by FRANCE 24 International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says learned of Trump's 'energy ceasefire' through media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e0663dfe5c3f6f3e6527da3897df5ae9c36e8a090da593f1f41b55b51b92083</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:24:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media--eb569c8092c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media" /><summary type="html">An Axios report is citing an unnamed US source who says that Donald Trump's surprise energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine only concerns oil refineries. Elitsa Gadeva explains what this would mean for both sides.</summary></entry><entry><title>Prison 'Games of Hope' olympics in Italy unite inmates and staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f592bf745f449b48fa68fd722d0bcb5db65f2f9c35f430159d09859d12afc85f</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:54:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff--1ade90bb6eaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff" /><summary type="html">Sport has the power to unite, and overcome barriers... In Rome, inmates and prison officers became athletes for the day, and took part in a sort of mini prison olympics. Organised by the John Paul II foundation for sport, this is the third edition of the “Games of Hope”, over a year after it was held in the men's wing of the prison in 2025. Story by Emily Boyle.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland: Police foils alleged assassination attempt against PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a22fc0e80a2eca304f06b04c76c9271f947d1ac1d3d0d16f210b77216adc4ff4</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:52:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-police-foils-alleged-assassination-attempt-against-pm--e367cf0a729f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-police-foils-alleged-assassination-attempt-against-pm" /><summary type="html">Poland's interior ministry said Sunday a man had been detained on suspicion of plotting an attack against Prime Minister Donald Tusk and Defence minister Wladyslaw Kosiniak-Kamysz. Interior minister Marcin Kierwinski told Polish media that the suspect, a man in his 60s, had been arrested in the southwestern region of Lower Silesia. He was identified through an analysis of content posted online. The man's home is being searched and his contacts examined. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Warsaw, Adrien Sarlat.</summary></entry><entry><title>Are European automakers capable of withstanding Chinese competition?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c8dcad14739eee3e16966df856bea47fd9b8d51634145364ab6d024130dadb9</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:26:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/are-european-automakers-capable-of-withstanding-chinese-competition--242508336086.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/are-european-automakers-capable-of-withstanding-chinese-competition" /><summary type="html">The Paris Motor Show opens its doors today, and with it come mounting economic and diplomatic issues. The European Union has just announced that it has secured a commitment from China to moderate the flow of hybrid vehicles into the block's market. It opens the prospect of cutting China's export by more than a half and could prevent millions of Chinese cars from being shipped to Europe. Are European automakers capable of withstanding this competition and their dependence on China? This report from France 2 and Morgan Ayre.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says surprised to hear about Trump's 'energy ceasefire' between Ukraine and Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8271944ec66ce51a119b32fa4802fc285c43df444537d87fe4f248d694d2ba41</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-surprised-to-hear-about-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-between-ukraine-and-russia--2d9571f46443.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-surprised-to-hear-about-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-between-ukraine-and-russia" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian power plants were hit by Russian strikes on Sunday, leading to power outages. President Volodymyr Zelensky announced the attacks and expressed his surprise at the US President's post that stated that an “energy ceasefire” had been agreed upon between Ukraine and Russia. While Zelensky said he was not aware of any deal he said he would welcome one. Moscow has yet to confirm any accord. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Americans Robert E. Hall and Michael Woodford win Nobel Prize in Economics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:068f971f6286190df0bc24cf82adf3ec8903ed20db5af417550b1c97618242ff</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:54:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-americans-robert-e-hall-and-michael-woodford-win-nobel-prize-in-economics--28f257b26685.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-americans-robert-e-hall-and-michael-woodford-win-nobel-prize-in-economics" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Nobel economics prize has been awarded to US economists ⁠Robert Hall ​and Michael Woodford, the Royal Swedish Academy of ‌Sciences said on Monday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump touts surprise 'energy ceasefire' – Zelensky says he hasn't seen details, Moscow silent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dac357bc2aa1684127e0f71b9809b4375b31c25b217fe01cd9f02d96d33ba30c</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-trump-touts-surprise-energy-ceasefire-_-zelensky-says-he-hasn-t-seen-details-moscow-silent--30ddc798f98c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-trump-touts-surprise-energy-ceasefire-%E2%80%93-zelensky-says-he-hasn-t-seen-details-moscow-silent" /><summary type="html">The US President Donald Trump sowed confusion on Sunday, announcing an "energy ceasefire" between Ukraine and Russia. Kyiv expressed astonishment, there was silence from Moscow. Ukrainian strikes have wreaked havoc on the Russian oil industry. Were there to be an "energy ceasefire" it could allow Moscow to repair refineries. For Ukraine, it could safeguard vital energy infrastructure. Story by Nicholas Rushworth.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia targets Ukraine energy facilities despite Trump ceasefire announcement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:501bb78b3a2f6ea34062dc7bf95548d488a9b642321205e35616aee0c1d41d36</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T05:29:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-live-oil-prices-fall-after-trump-unilaterally-announces-russia-ukraine-energy-ceasefire--87f1573e7c8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-live-oil-prices-fall-after-trump-unilaterally-announces-russia-ukraine-energy-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">Russia continued to attack multiple power plants in Ukraine on Monday, in spite of claims by US President Donald yesterday stating a so-called “energy ceasefire” had been agreed to. NATO chief said that the military alliance would “block, blunt and break” any Russian attack on its members’ territory. Meanwhile strikes on civilians continue, with a 13-year-old girl among three killed in the country's east. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO top commander to warn Russia over alliance’s ability to counter-attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42db20faf78c41205b67fc2649eef5d45e635d2ab03b9a6f2c6a464d61f981eb</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:41:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-top-commander-warn-russia-alliance-counter-attack--fa171fb255f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-top-commander-warn-russia-alliance-counter-attack" /><summary type="html">NATO’s top military commander is expected to warn Russia on Monday that the alliance can counter any attack, officials said. US General Alexus Grynkewich will outline his “theory of victory” at a Warsaw security conference amid Western concerns over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Ukraine’s wartime backers.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Slovenia rejects bill in blow to PM Janez Jansa’s reform agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbc9c0488c99e224a51bc1bc373994b953e2aa471a5715d859c3d1d0f894e4e5</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T22:01:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-slovenia-bill-pm-janez-jansa-reform--8369f436d303.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-slovenia-bill-pm-janez-jansa-reform" /><summary type="html">Slovenians rejected a bill expanding parliamentary inquiry powers in a referendum Sunday, dealing a blow to nationalist Prime Minister Janez Jansa. With 99 percent of votes counted, 51 percent opposed the proposal and 49 percent backed it in the binding vote. The opposition had denounced his reform agenda as "authoritarian".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham warns French voters of Russian political influence on back of Brexit vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a523290bb9e2a477702eb79b0095b20081d4458fcba1e3475dc6830c4c53e46a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T19:42:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-uk-pm-burnham-warns-french-voters-of-russian-political-influence-on-back-of-brexit-vote--49889e6c39bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-uk-pm-burnham-warns-french-voters-of-russian-political-influence-on-back-of-brexit-vote" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Sunday warned French and German voters of potential for Russian influence in upcoming elections, on the back of "clear" interference in Britain's referendum on European Union membership in 2016. Russia has previously denied meddling in the Brexit vote, while former British leader Boris Johnson 2020 also said there was no evidence of interference. Burnham made the comments in an interview with The Rest is Politics podcast, released on Sunday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Coerced into a corner?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dceb51e4fe63665f074fae723b8e0240261ac4c16501ef73a2cebcaba3d7dc55</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T17:36:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261011-ukraine-coerced-into-a-corner--d1fdea5bcd74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261011-ukraine-coerced-into-a-corner" /><summary type="html">It's reported that Ukraine is right now facing intense diplomatic pressure and coercion from the Trump administration to end the war quickly.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>New Russian strikes follow Trump's announcement of Russia-Ukraine energy ceasefire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c72be90d017a0c8813dd469cfa64bf786f13838029513516309d67d5897ab5ec</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:39:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire--acf7a15a4061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">US President Trump said Sunday via social media platform Truth Social that Russia and Ukraine had agreed to an energy ceasefire. Neither Kyiv nor Moscow confirmed the agreement, but Zelensky later confirmed new Russian strikes to a Ukrainian powerplant. Additional reports suggest at least 5 have been killed and other civilians injured in strikes in the cities of Kharkiv and Ivano-Frankivsk.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: French student protests, October 7 anniversary and Adenot's return to Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05e03dc5a86086bc6cfca38651b7536c13964f569ace89341cf749a05d69c049</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T13:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-ear--92c20302aefd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-earth" /><summary type="html">Blockades and protests by French secondary school and university students continued, occasionally becoming violent; French astronaut Sophie Adenot returned to Earth after eight months aboard the International Space Station; Israel's commemorations marking the three-year anniversary of the October 7 attacks: here's a look back at some of the most striking images from the past week's news.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo says will undergo surgery for early-stage lung nodule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec4cb8c1ab7b64a1c9c174cf6d08c78571fa397bc14bc82d704783ff032cbad</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T10:34:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-pope-leo-says-will-undergo-surgery-for-early-stage-lung-nodule--110af765b1d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-pope-leo-says-will-undergo-surgery-for-early-stage-lung-nodule" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV said Sunday he would undergo surgery in the coming days for a lung nodule detected at an early stage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says ready to halt refinery strikes if Moscow stops energy attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc47504440a7a052b6152c05d447123664256317cd26f088c1f821db18cf32a6</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T10:21:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-ukraine-ready-halt-refinery-strikes-if-moscow-stops-energy-attacks-zelensky-says--6653602e82d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-ukraine-ready-halt-refinery-strikes-if-moscow-stops-energy-attacks-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Sunday said Kyiv was ready to halt strikes Russian oil refineries if Moscow stopped attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure. Zelensky also pushed back on US President Donald Trump's comments made Saturday evening calling for Ukraine to elect a new leader by saying, "It's up to our people".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez kicks off election campaign amid housing crisis protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca69604a914b4ae59d33aecf78e93c362e5271e01bbec29afe9f0886fb80211c</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-spanish-pm-sanchez-kicks-off-election-campaign-amid-housing-crisis-protests--31069b0fb951.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-spanish-pm-sanchez-kicks-off-election-campaign-amid-housing-crisis-protests" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez launched his campaign for a snap November election on Saturday. The vote comes as a deepening housing crisis is driving protests and putting pressure on his left-wing coalition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Zelensky clash over diesel deal as Russian strikes on Ukraine kill at least 21</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a954a921c6fafdaa8393839816ddff03c8e366572bd7c58b6366779d770e1c6</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-child--ee33fd4d2e87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-children" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday told reporters that Ukraine should "get a new president", adding that his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky had disobeyed his orders not to strike Russian refineries. This came after Washington moved to ease sanctions on Russian diesel and as Moscow's strikes on Ukraine, including the city of Zaporizhzhia, killed at least 21 people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
